This private stage repairs ownership in the exported data-pack writer copied from the exact frozen main candidate. The unchanged helper `c68d66ff24d99d07f26e318675d11138946fdc5fa858d46ff6f4032a754cd1b3` has a preserved held-commit reproduction: save(B) resolves during flush(A), then the flush discards B without committing it. Current application capture awaits save and flush sequentially; application or HTTP data loss has not been demonstrated.

Public save, flush and dispose acquire the same private operation flag synchronously. A call while another public operation owns the writer rejects with `ERR_RESTIC_DATA_PACK_BUSY` before guard checks, hashing, allocation, queue mutation or disposal. Save awaits a private flush without trying to reacquire ownership. The flag clears in finally on every settled success or failure. Read-only count and has remain usable. Disposal is synchronous and still means discard pending data; it is not a terminal writer shutdown. An encrypted incoming payload which has not entered the queue is wiped if automatic flushing or its subsequent guard check rejects. Existing queue payload cleanup and primary-error poisoning on a failed flush remain intact. Caller-owned source buffers and independently allocated committed pack bytes are not wiped.

Tests will hold the actual commit callback for save versus flush, flush versus flush, dispose during an active operation, and save versus save while a preceding queued pack is flushed automatically. Rejected calls must not change queue membership or issue commits. Releasing the rightful owner must commit every subsequently accepted unique byte sequence once, with authenticated pack headers, contiguous offsets, index entries and plaintext hashes independently decoded. Held commit rejection must retain the original Error, release ownership, clear and zero the old queue and the unqueued incoming ciphertext. A child-local Buffer.concat observer may retain ciphertext allocation references to check this last buffer property; its hook will be restored in finally. This is finite functional testing, not a memory measurement or full erasure claim.

Run the unchanged nine helper tests and focused capture, deadline and lifecycle tests against the private stage, plus new independent held-callback regressions. Record exact source hashes before and after, bounded raw output and attempt failures. Preserve the full old 250/214-file inventories by reference and reauthentication without reclassifying their 66/33 historical tests as a new run. No original executable invocation is needed to test an application helper ownership rule; the independently verified original format comparisons remain historical and unchanged. No production integration, publication, timing or memory benchmark is authorized here.
